# SysML Parallel TVCache — project agent rules

Teammate-facing docs: root `README.md` only. Exp A evidence write-ups: `docs/workload_characterization_report.md` (A0) · `_A1.md` · `_A2.md` (pilots). Experiments A/B/C via `bash scripts/run_experiment.sh {none|sequential|parallel|all}` (only `none` implemented today; mode picks one experiment unless `all`). Exp B sequential TVCache can proceed in parallel (stub until tvclient wired).

## Deployment boundaries

- NERSC is inference-only. Harbor / Pi / task / verifier run on the Mac via Docker.
- Use only m4999 (`--account=m4999 --constraint=gpu`). Never ntrain5.
- Proven A0 alloc: 1 GPU, 32 CPUs, 56G, `shared_interactive`. A1: 4 GPUs, TP=4, ~220G, often `interactive` QOS. Preferred later 9B serve: **2 GPUs / TP=2**, ~120G, `interactive` (A2 TP2 pilot). Release promptly; `scancel` on backend death or Mac runner stall.
- FlashInfer workaround until retested: node-local JIT caches + `VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0`.
- Valid vLLM flag: `--default-chat-template-kwargs`. Qwen3.5 text DeepSWE: `--language-model-only` (+ `--reasoning-parser qwen3` when thinking off).
- Live runs need fresh MFA: `sshproxy -u <user> -f` (browser / Iris federated login). Prefer Terminal.app / `screen -dmS … bash scripts/…` over Cursor-shell `nohup` (Cursor can reap the process group while orphan Docker/Slurm keep going).
- Harbor Pi custom endpoint needs host env `OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18081/v1` + `OPENAI_API_KEY=EMPTY` (set in `run_harbor_wave.sh`). Omitting it yields `model_api requires an explicitly configured base URL` and zero sessions — quarantine those job dirs and re-run.
- Resume a live NERSC serve with `SYSML_ATTACH_JOB` + `SYSML_ATTACH_NODE` (after `bridge_up` is defined). Do not `scancel` a READY alloc just because the Mac runner died.
- Default wave: `SYSML_PASS_K=5`, `SYSML_HARBOR_N=5`, `SYSML_MAX_NUM_SEQS=5`, `SYSML_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.80`, tasks from `configs/experiment-tasks.txt` (10 setup variants). Recycle alloc every `SYSML_TASKS_PER_ALLOC` (default 2). GPU monitor: `scripts/monitor_nersc_gpu.sh` / `gpu-monitor.log`.
- Do not confuse knobs: `SYSML_MAX_MODEL_LEN` / `SYSML_CONTEXT_WINDOW` = total prompt+history capacity; `SYSML_MAX_TOKENS` = **per-completion** generation cap; `SYSML_MAX_TURNS` = assistant **turn** ceiling (not tokens). Reward 0 + turn exhaustion ≠ “ran out of 256K context.”
- Exp A on **Qwen3.5-9B** closed for capability: **A0+A1+A2 pilots** all reward **0** (see `docs/workload_characterization_report_A2.md`). Prefer **TP=2** at 256K; thinking=high best F2P (~7/82) still no solve. **Next capability:** stronger model (~27B / Qwen3.x — Hub id TBD). Harbor rejects bare `thinking=on` (use `high`). Mac Docker: 2×n=5 bind/subnet races → `TASK_PARALLEL=1` or n≤3; `SYSML_TASK_STAGGER_SEC` available. Prefer Terminal.app `.local-smoke/*.command` (Cursor reap → EXIT `scancel`). Historical `char-setup-9b-t8v2` was 3 tasks × n=1 — do not conflate. On OOM add GPUs / shorten len / lower seqs; on Docker bind races fall back to `N=1`. Fresh `sshproxy` required before any live wave.

## Evidence honesty

- Reward 0 + `exception_info=null` is graded unsuccessful, not infra success by itself.
- Inspect Pi session + verifier; do not invent rewards or manufacture parallelism.
- Preserve `jobs/` / `results/` evidence. Never commit `.local-smoke/` or `.env`.

## Characterization

- Handout Experiment A uses `variants/deep-swe-setup/` (setup in instruction). Do not edit `vendor/deep-swe/tasks/` in place.
- Parallel-turn fraction = turns with >1 emitted call / all assistant turns (incl. zero-call).
- Analyze with `bash scripts/analyze_characterization_wave.sh <prefix>` — do not glob unrelated `jobs/`.
- TVCache key = trajectory prefix in the TCG. Paper win = cross-rollout reuse (Exp B). Within-turn N>1 is Exp C.

## Model / runner sync

- When changing model id, update sbatch, gateway `--model`, `SYSML_MODEL_ID`, LoopbackPi, and Harbor `-m` together.
- Active model: `Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B` (tool parser `qwen3_coder`). Stronger-model swap is next capability cell — keep all id touchpoints in sync.
